{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QHeatEquation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QHeatEquation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation.classicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation.classicalLimit","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L49-L56","doc":"Classical heat equation is the `q = 1` specialisation.  Over\n`R_q = ℤ[T; T⁻¹]`, evaluating at `q = 1` sends each monomial\n`T^n ↦ 1`, so the value is the sum of all Laurent coefficients\n(`LaurentPolynomial ℤ = ℤ →₀ ℤ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation.evolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation.evolves","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The evolution equation: `∂ₜ u(t,x) = Δ_q u(t,x)` pointwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation.dq_u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation.dq_u","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L45-L45","doc":"q-Laplacian applied to `u`: `Δ_q u : ℝ → S → R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation.dt_u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation.dt_u","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Time-derivative `∂ₜ u : ℝ → S → R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation.u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation.u","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Time-dependent section `u : ℝ → S → R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation","kind":"structure","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L32-L47","doc":"**q-Heat equation data**: a one-parameter family of sections `u t`\ntogether with the q-Laplacian `Δ_q`, satisfying `∂ₜ u = Δ_q u`.\n\nEncoded abstractly as a predicate on the pair (time-derivative,\nq-Laplacian-value) — this is the algebraic shadow of the PDE,\nindependent of any analytic choice of differentiability. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-heat-equation","label":"def:q-heat-equation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0}]}